CAPI=2:
# Copyright 2026 Serge Rabyking
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# The VLNV carries no package version. It restated one, and by the
# time anyone looked it said 0.1.0 against a package that had
# reached 0.5.0 -- a second copy of a number pyproject.toml owns.
# Everything this project GENERATES already names itself :0.
name: lanserge:np2hw:gen:0
description: >
  np2hw as a FuseSoC generator: trace a NumPy model file into synthesisable
  Verilog at build time, or build a pipeline of blocks into its verified
  design pack. The model file follows the CLI convention -- it exposes
  model() (or file.py:func) and optionally PARAMS. Requires np2hw on the
  PATH (pip install np2hw).

generators:
  np2hw:
    command: np2hw-fusesoc
    description: >
      Trace a NumPy model into a Verilog core. Parameters: model (path to
      the .py, relative to the calling core), width, height, bits (input
      image geometry, required), module_name (optional). Or build a
      pipeline: design (package.module:name; the calling core's folder is
      a library root), control, clock_mhz, verify, sync_memory.
